<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Main Results</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S5.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 5 Results and Analysis ‣ GoiBERT: Compact Vietnamese Language Models via Two-Stage Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> compares GoiBERT with existing Vietnamese and
multilingual encoders.
We highlight three findings.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">GoiBERT-large is the strongest non-teacher model.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">GoiBERT-large reaches an average of 81.13, ahead of PhoBERT-v2 (80.71)
and BamiBERT (80.65), and it is the best non-teacher model on five of
the eight tasks.
The largest gains over BamiBERT, its Stage-1 teacher, appear on
fine-grained sentiment: <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math>2.47 pair F1 on ABSA-Restaurant and <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math>1.73
on ABSA-Hotel, followed by <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math>1.54 macro-F1 on VSFC-Topic.
Thus a student with 48% of BamiBERT’s parameters does not merely
approximate its teacher but outperforms it on most tasks.
The improvement comes from the second, CafeBERT-guided stage
(§<a href="#S5.SS4" title="5.4 Ablation Study ‣ 5 Results and Analysis ‣ GoiBERT: Compact Vietnamese Language Models via Two-Stage Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>).
The full 15-metric average gives the same ordering: 84.02 for
GoiBERT-large, 83.61 for BamiBERT, and 82.98 for GoiBERT-base
(Table <a href="#A2.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Layer-wise learning-rate decay. ‣ Appendix B Distillation Details ‣ GoiBERT: Compact Vietnamese Language Models via Two-Stage Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">GoiBERT-base is a strong extreme-efficiency point.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With only 26.4M parameters and 4.8 GFLOPs, GoiBERT-base averages
80.02, which is 99.2% of BamiBERT’s average with a quarter of its size.
It still outperforms BamiBERT on both UIT-ABSA domains and on
VSFC-Topic, and it exceeds ViSoBERT and XLM-R-base on average despite
being 3.7<math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> and 10.5<math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> smaller, respectively.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">The cost of compression is task-dependent.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">GoiBERT does not lead everywhere.
BamiBERT remains better on ViNLI (<math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>−</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-</annotation></semantics></math>1.66 for GoiBERT-large) and
PhoNER (<math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>−</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-</annotation></semantics></math>0.85).
PhoBERT-v2 is best among non-teacher models on PhoNER and
VSFC-Sentiment, although on PhoNER it benefits from external word
segmentation, which GoiBERT does not use.
We analyze these patterns next.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
