<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Architecture and Initialization</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A1.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Appendix A Architecture and Initialization ‣ GoiBERT: Compact Vietnamese Language Models via Two-Stage Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> provides a layer-level view of
the GoiBERT encoder family.
The model configurations are summarized in §<a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Compact Architecture ‣ 3 GoiBERT ‣ GoiBERT: Compact Vietnamese Language Models via Two-Stage Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>; here we
provide the additional implementation details omitted from the main paper.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For GoiBERT-large, the word embeddings are initialized from BamiBERT’s
768-dimensional embedding matrix using principal component analysis
(PCA), retaining the leading 512 components.
The projected embeddings are normalized and rescaled to match the
standard deviation of the student’s embedding initialization.
Transformer blocks are initialized randomly.
Both variants use BamiBERT’s tokenizer and support up to 2,050 position
embeddings; general distillation uses sequences of at most 256 tokens.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F4" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2610.30067v1/GoiBERT_Architecture_Final.svg" id="A1.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:381/725;" width="381" height="725"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>
Detailed encoder architecture of GoiBERT-base and GoiBERT-large.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Distillation Details</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section expands the matching terms used in the general-distillation
objective in Eq. <a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.2 Stage 1: General Distillation ‣ 3 GoiBERT ‣ GoiBERT: Compact Vietnamese Language Models via Two-Stage Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> (§<a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Stage 1: General Distillation ‣ 3 GoiBERT ‣ GoiBERT: Compact Vietnamese Language Models via Two-Stage Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>) and the optimization
schedule used during task-specific distillation.
Let <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\{\mathrm{base},\mathrm{large}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>base</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>large</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\{\mathrm{base},\mathrm{large}\}</annotation></semantics></math> index a GoiBERT variant,
and let <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> denote its number of Transformer layers,
hidden dimension, and number of attention heads, respectively.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Hidden-state matching.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a sequence of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> tokens, let
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\ell}^{v}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d_{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\ell}^{v}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d_{v}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the student hidden states
at layer <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=0</annotation></semantics></math> denoting the embedding output.
Let <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\pi_{v}(\ell)}^{B}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times 768}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>768</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\pi_{v}(\ell)}^{B}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times 768}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the hidden
states of the aligned BamiBERT teacher layer.
The function <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{v}(\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{v}(\ell)</annotation></semantics></math> specifies which teacher layer is paired with
student layer <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Layer mapping.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Hidden-state distillation needs one teacher target for every student
layer.
For GoiBERT-large, both encoders have 12 Transformer layers, so the
mapping is one-to-one: <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{large}}(\ell)=\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>large</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{large}}(\ell)=\ell</annotation></semantics></math> for
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=0,\ldots,12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=0,\ldots,12</annotation></semantics></math>.
GoiBERT-base has 10 layers and cannot be paired one-to-one with the 12
teacher layers, so we use a layer mapping
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{base}}:\{0,\ldots,10\}\rightarrow\{0,\ldots,12\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>base</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>12</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{base}}:\{0,\ldots,10\}\rightarrow\{0,\ldots,12\}</annotation></semantics></math> that
selects 10 of the teacher’s hidden states as targets.
The mapping fixes <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{base}}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>base</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{base}}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, so that student and teacher
embedding outputs are aligned, and it is strictly increasing, so that
the depth order of the teacher is preserved: each student layer
imitates a teacher layer at a comparable stage of processing, and the
two unselected teacher layers receive no matching term.
This follows the layer-mapping strategy of TinyBERT
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiao et al. (2020)</a></cite>, where a shallower student learns from a
subset of teacher layers.
In our implementation, the selected teacher layers are
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl(\pi_{\mathrm{base}}(1),\ldots,\pi_{\mathrm{base}}(10)\bigr)=(1,2,4,5,6,7,8,10,11,12)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>base</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>base</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>12</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(\pi_{\mathrm{base}}(1),\ldots,\pi_{\mathrm{base}}(10)\bigr)=(1,2,4,5,6,7,8,10,11,12)</annotation></semantics></math>, together with <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{base}}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>base</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{base}}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>
for the embedding outputs.
GoiBERT-base therefore skips teacher layers 3 and 9, while the
remaining layers keep the teacher’s depth order.
Each student hidden state is mapped from 384 to 768 dimensions by its
own learned linear projection, and the attention-matching term below
uses the same Transformer-layer alignment.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Because the hidden dimensions differ, a trainable linear projection
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\ell}^{v}:\mathbb{R}^{d_{v}}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{768}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>768</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\ell}^{v}:\mathbb{R}^{d_{v}}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{768}</annotation></semantics></math> maps the
student representation to the teacher space before comparison.
The hidden-state term is</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{hid}}=\frac{1}{L_{v}+1}\sum_{\ell=0}^{L_{v}}\operatorname{MSE}_{\mathrm{nonpad}}\!\bigl(P^{v}_{\ell}(H^{v}_{\ell}),\,H^{B}_{\pi_{v}(\ell)}\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>hid</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>MSE</mi><mi>nonpad</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{hid}}=\frac{1}{L_{v}+1}\sum_{\ell=0}^{L_{v}}\operatorname{MSE}_{\mathrm{nonpad}}\!\bigl(P^{v}_{\ell}(H^{v}_{\ell}),\,H^{B}_{\pi_{v}(\ell)}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{MSE}_{\mathrm{nonpad}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>MSE</mi><mi>nonpad</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{MSE}_{\mathrm{nonpad}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes mean-squared error evaluated only at non-padding token positions. Padding tokens therefore do not contribute to the loss. The projection layers are optimized jointly with the student encoder, while BamiBERT remains frozen.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Attention matching.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The student and teacher also use different numbers of attention heads.
Direct head-to-head matching would therefore be undefined.
Instead, we average the post-softmax attention probabilities within
each layer before comparing the two models.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\ell,h}^{m}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\ell,h}^{m}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>
be the attention probability matrix produced by head <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> of layer
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> in model <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of attention heads
in that model.
We define the head-averaged attention matrix as</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{A}_{\ell}^{m}=\frac{1}{a_{m}}\sum_{h=1}^{a_{m}}A_{\ell,h}^{m}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></munderover><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{A}_{\ell}^{m}=\frac{1}{a_{m}}\sum_{h=1}^{a_{m}}A_{\ell,h}^{m}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Each entry of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{A}_{\ell}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{A}_{\ell}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> therefore represents the average
attention probability assigned from one token position to another
across all heads in that layer.
The attention-matching term is</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{att}}^{v}=\dfrac{1}{L_{v}}\sum_{\ell=1}^{L_{v}}\operatorname{MSE}\left(\bar{A}_{\ell}^{v},\bar{A}_{\pi_{v}(\ell)}^{B}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>att</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><mi>MSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{att}}^{v}=\dfrac{1}{L_{v}}\sum_{\ell=1}^{L_{v}}\operatorname{MSE}\left(\bar{A}_{\ell}^{v},\bar{A}_{\pi_{v}(\ell)}^{B}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The summation starts at the first Transformer layer because the
embedding output has no self-attention matrix.
The hidden-state and attention terms in
Eqs. <a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3.2 Stage 1: General Distillation ‣ 3 GoiBERT ‣ GoiBERT: Compact Vietnamese Language Models via Two-Stage Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>–<a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3.2 Stage 1: General Distillation ‣ 3 GoiBERT ‣ GoiBERT: Compact Vietnamese Language Models via Two-Stage Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> are combined as
specified by Eq. <a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.2 Stage 1: General Distillation ‣ 3 GoiBERT ‣ GoiBERT: Compact Vietnamese Language Models via Two-Stage Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> in the main paper.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Out-of-fold soft supervision.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The task-specific objective itself is defined in
Eq. <a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3.3 Stage 2: Out-of-Fold Task Distillation ‣ 3 GoiBERT ‣ GoiBERT: Compact Vietnamese Language Models via Two-Stage Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.
Here we clarify how its CafeBERT soft targets are produced.
The task training set is divided into five folds.
For fold <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, a CafeBERT teacher is fine-tuned on the other four folds
and used only to predict examples in the held-out fold.
Repeating this procedure over all five folds gives one soft target for
every training example without allowing its teacher to train on that
example.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The resulting CafeBERT logits are converted to temperature-scaled
probabilities as defined in Eq. <a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3.3 Stage 2: Out-of-Fold Task Distillation ‣ 3 GoiBERT ‣ GoiBERT: Compact Vietnamese Language Models via Two-Stage Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, using
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>.
For ABSA, distillation is applied independently to each aspect slot.
For NER, CafeBERT soft targets are aligned with the first subword of
each original syllable.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Layer-wise learning-rate decay.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">During task-specific fine-tuning, lower encoder layers receive
progressively smaller updates.
Let <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> denote the task-level base learning rate and let
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=1,\ldots,L_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=1,\ldots,L_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> index Transformer layers from bottom to top.
The learning rate assigned to layer <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\ell}=\eta\,\gamma^{L_{v}-\ell},\qquad\gamma=0.8." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\ell}=\eta\,\gamma^{L_{v}-\ell},\qquad\gamma=0.8.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, the top Transformer layer receives <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, while layers closer
to the embedding layer receive increasingly smaller rates.
The embedding parameters use <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\gamma^{L_{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\gamma^{L_{v}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the task-specific
head uses the full base rate <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T5" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A2.T5.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A2.T5.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T5.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Task</span></th>
