<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Training and Measurement Details</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">General distillation is run for 120,000 optimization steps with batch
size 32 and sequence length 256.
We use AdamW with learning rate <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>, weight decay <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math>,
1,000 warmup steps, and linear learning-rate decay.
This stage uses seed 42 and bfloat16 precision on one NVIDIA L40S GPU.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For downstream tasks, both GoiBERT variants are fine-tuned for
30 epochs with batch size 32 using AdamW, weight decay <math id="A4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math>, and
10% warmup.
The base learning rate is <math id="A4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math> for the two UIT-VSFC tasks,
<math id="A4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math> for ViSpamReviews, and <math id="A4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> for the remaining
tasks.
GoiBERT additionally uses the layer-wise decay in
Eq. <a href="#A2.E6" title="In Layer-wise learning-rate decay. ‣ Appendix B Distillation Details ‣ GoiBERT: Compact Vietnamese Language Models via Two-Stage Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.
For the rerun BamiBERT baseline, the learning rate is selected from
<math id="A4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{10^{-5},2\times 10^{-5},5\times 10^{-5}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{10^{-5},2\times 10^{-5},5\times 10^{-5}\}</annotation></semantics></math> using validation
performance; BamiBERT is trained with cross-entropy only.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Model selection is based exclusively on validation data.
Reported local test results are averaged over fine-tuning seeds
42, 43, and 44.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Efficiency measurements use the encoder only.
GPU throughput and peak VRAM are measured on an NVIDIA L40S using
bfloat16 and scaled-dot-product attention at batch size 32 and sequence
length 256.
CPU latency is measured in float32 with eight CPU threads for a single
128-token input.
Timing measurements use repeated forward passes after warm-up; the
same measurement protocol is applied to all compared encoders.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Complete Benchmark Results</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A2.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Layer-wise learning-rate decay. ‣ Appendix B Distillation Details ‣ GoiBERT: Compact Vietnamese Language Models via Two-Stage Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> provides the complete set of 15 test metrics,
together with parameter counts and estimated computational cost.
The 15-metric average is reported only as a descriptive summary:
the metrics have different interpretations, and tasks contributing two
metrics receive greater weight than PhoNER, which contributes one.
The GoiBERT–BamiBERT comparison also reflects the complete downstream
training pipelines rather than architecture alone, since GoiBERT uses
CafeBERT distillation and layer-wise learning-rate decay whereas the
rerun BamiBERT baseline uses standard cross-entropy fine-tuning.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
